Saturate branch/match after via UnderProd

The after-structure of a `branch` or `match` was previously a noop clone
of the before-structure, with no morphisms tying it to the branch ends.
This change turns the after-structure into the meet of the branch ends
in the lattice of extensions of the before-structure  equivalently, the
product in the under-category `before/Struct`. Concretely the
after-structure now receives every equality, pred_app and func_app that
holds in every branch/case end.

The mechanics:

  - `StructureCat` gains an `under_prods: Vec<UnderProd>` registry
    pairing each `meet` with its `top` and the list of `end_i`s. The
    `top -> meet` and `meet -> end_i` morphisms live in the existing
    `morphisms` map; the registry is what tells the close pass which
    structures to saturate.

  - `StructureCat::close` now iterates forward + backward + saturate to
    a fixed point. Saturation pulls equalities, pred_apps and func_apps
    from the ends back into the meet whenever the fact holds in every
    end. Func_app saturation may allocate a fresh meet element for the
    result and extends each `meet -> end_i` projection accordingly.

  - `algebra::populate` pre-allocates the after-structure for `branch`
    and `match` before walking the bodies, so the projection morphisms
    `meet -> end_i` point forward in the arena. `Branch` and `Match`
    both use `MorphismKind::Noop` for the `top -> meet` morphism now;
    `Match` previously used `If` which was a misnomer (the existential
    element from the scrutinee lives in `match_after_scrutinee`, not in
    the after-stmt structure).

  - `push_morphism` now canonicalises ElMap values through the target's
    unification, not just the keys through the source's. Without this,
    repeated push calls in the new fixed-point loop would re-insert
    pred_app/func_app entries with stale element ids and never report
    `changed = false`.
